WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.135
-Simu, welcome to the show.

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for having me, Jimmy.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:04.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, my God, best --

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.439 size:88% position:44%
Can I just say best swag

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
of any talk show
or any I´ve ever been?

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I mean, look at the detail.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:11.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Look at that.
-First of all, you know,

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:14.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
shrinkwrapped,
shrinkwrapped, ribboned mugs.

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.717
-Shrink wrapped, ribboned mugs
filled with water, by the way.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
That´s very hard to do.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.587 size:81% position:41%
-It´s very hard to do.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.822 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, I mean, you could
use that for anything.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:25.825 size:84% position:42%
-You are my parents´
favorite talk show host

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so, they will be
enjoying this.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience awws ]
So I´m bringing this home.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:32.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, Mom and Dad, I love you.
Hi.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:35.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheering and applause ]
And, yeah.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´ve got to be very proud
of your son.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Don´t let me forget that.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
I won´t.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.841 size:75% position:38%
How are you feeling?

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.177
This is the biggest movie
in the world right now.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:47.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
Shattered records, made
over $160 million worldwide.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, man.
-Yeah. I mean,

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I know all these numbers.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I´m a numbers guy.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
How does it feel?

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you picture
this moment happening?

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
I probably pictured it

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a little less COVID,
to be honest.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, of course. Yeah.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.863 size:88% position:44%
-You know? Like a little
less social distancing,

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:06.299
a little less lockdown,
quarantine, and all that.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I feel like --
[ Laughs ]

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.536
I feel like it´s an exercise

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
in lowering your
expectations, right?

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.873
Because I mean, it´s, you know,
we did well, it´s a lot of money

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it´s the number 1 movie
in the world.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.211
But, you know, Marvel movies
make like billions of dollars

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:21.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the fact that like
we have ours

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:25.151
and it made, you know, 160 --
which is great, amazing, right?

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:27.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
But like they usually make
$1 billion, so, then --

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, but, I mean,

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
you´re handling it very well
-Thank you.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:34.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
-and you have
a good sense of humor,

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.362 size:88% position:44%
but also, high pressure.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:40.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
You threw out the first pitch,
which I´m afraid to do.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yes.
-Really, I don´t know
if I ever will do it

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.471
because it´s just so much --

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:47.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m so nervous
and I´m not a pitcher.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And so, you know.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you went out,
San Francisco Giants,

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you threw out
the first pitch.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.047 size:78% position:39%
Not only great pitch,

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
but then you did
the coolest thing after --

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.784
you did a full-on backflip.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Little backflip
situation, yeah.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.554
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Why add the pressure?

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:04.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why? Once you got the pitch
down, then you go,

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:05.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Clap ] "I´m outta here.
We´re good.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
Peace out."
-Well, that´s the thing,

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:11.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that I didn´t expect the
pitch to go as well as it did.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And, when I actually threw it,
it went like

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
straight down the line.
It was a strike.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.503
I mean, it was a strike going
at like two miles per hour.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Doesn´t matter. It counts.

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I was so happy
in that moment, I was like,

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah! We want to do it!"
You know?

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.309 size:84% position:42%
I wouldn´t necessarily
have done the backflip,

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.044
if I had just thrown the ball

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it just bounced
off the ground

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:28.548 size:84% position:42%
or something like that.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was amazing.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
Questlove,
our very own Questlove has --

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:33.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.655
-Has thrown out the first pitch
at a Phillies game.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:38.124
-I´ve seen this legendary video.
-Yeah, he´s at a Phillies game.

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:39.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
He threw out the first pitch.
We actually have

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
a clip of Questlove

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
throwing the first pitch.
-Let´s take a look.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:43.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it´s pretty good.
Take a look at this.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:46.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the pitch.

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:49.068
-♫ Here I come, here I come ♫

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, yeah, terrible, yeah.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:54.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheering, laughter,
and applause ]

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just walked out.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just left.
He just walked out.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just left the building.
-Where´d he go?

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:05.218 size:81% position:41%
-He left. It´s a very
difficult thing to do.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:07.620 size:88% position:44%
High pressure and, yeah,
not everyone can do it.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
I appreciate that.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to talk
about "Shang-Chi."

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:13.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:15.161 size:84% position:42%
-What does it feel like

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:19.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be kind of looked up to,
now, of kids --

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:22.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
as well as adults,
but kids seeing you

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:25.171
as an action hero, a superhero?

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was it like
to play that role?

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.877
-I mean, you know, first of all,
it was a dream come true

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know, growing up,
I´d been such a big fan

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.416 size:75% position:38%
of superhero movies,
cartoons, TV shows.

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:37.917
Like I watched all of them.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.385
I watched like the stuff that,

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:42.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, even like,
you know, the Jessica Alba,

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:44.324
you know, "Fantastic Four"
from all the way back when

00:03:44.324 --> 00:03:46.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all the obscure
Marvel movies.

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Punisher,"
I was probably not allowed

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.362
to watch it at the time,
but I watched it, anyway.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:50.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You know, I just --

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:53.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I loved
what superheroes represented,

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:57.503
which is this kind of hope
and this unlimited possibility.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.173
And I just feel like everybody,
regardless of, you know,

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.175 size:88% position:44%
the color of their skin
or where they come from,

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.644
deserves to see themselves
represented in that way.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.446
So what I´m really excited
about this movie is that

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:10.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
we get to provide that
for kids everywhere, you know,

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheering and applause ]
and to be something

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:15.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I never had growing up.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:18.458 size:84% position:42%
Did you ever see anyone
that looked like you

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a superhero growing up,
or who did you...?

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:24.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, you know,
I loved Spider-Man

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Spider-Man had a whole,
you know,

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.433
a full mask over his face

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:31.738
and so you could kind of imagine
who was underneath.

00:04:31.738 --> 00:04:34.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we had
the occasional Power Ranger.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Do you watch "Power Rangers"?

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I did watch
"Power Rangers."

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, I mean, it´s a big deal.
It´s a big deal.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.148
-Please take the moment in

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
and know what you mean
to a lot of people.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.285
It´s really changed the game...

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-...in a great way.

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, congratulations on that.
-See that, Mom?

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah, no, exactly.

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:51.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´m doing okay.

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jimmy says I´m doing okay,
I´m doing okay.

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:55.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Beyond okay.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.964
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here´s Simu Liu

00:04:57.964 --> 00:05:00.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
in "Shang-Chi and the Legend
of the Ten Rings."

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.701 size:75% position:38%
Take a look at this.

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.469 line:0%
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:07.273 size:88% position:44%
-You have the wrong guy!

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:08.708
Does he look like he can fight?!

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:09.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
Come on, bro!

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:12.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh!

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ahh!

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
♫♫

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:20.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
You okay?

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:23.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Grunting ]

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:33.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
♫♫

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:36.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
♫♫

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:37.337 size:75% position:38%
-Yo, what up, y´all?

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:38.504 size:75% position:38%
It´s your boy Cliff,

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
coming at you live on the bus.

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:43.643
I actually did take a little bit
of martial arts as a youth,

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:46.145
so I´m going to try and grade
this fight as we´re going.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:52.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
♫♫

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:56.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheering and applause ]
-More with Simu Liu
